BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Buncombe Age-Friendly Senior Centers
SUMMARY:Health Education Leading to Prevention (HELP) Program
LOCATION:Linwood Crump Shiloh Community Center\, 121 Shiloh Road\, Ashev
 ille
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T130000
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:FALSE
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Event Type";ID=21;TYPE=number:Default Templat
 e
DTSTAMP:20221128T170914Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>Health Education Leading to Prevention (HELP) Program - 
 The third and fourth Wednesdays\, 12 pm - 1 pm. In partnership with Shil
 oh Community Association\, IFPHA\, and Avery Health Education &amp\; Con
 sulting LLC led by Kathey Avery\, these classes focus on the self-manage
 ment of chronic disease and diabetes as well as maintaining a healthy an
 d well-balanced lifestyle. No pre-registration required.
CATEGORIES:Age Friendly
UID:http://uid.trumba.com/event/163413343
X-TRUMBA-LINK:https://www.buncombecounty.org/governing/depts/dss/adults/
 age-friendly.aspx?trumbaEmbed=view%3Devent%26eventid%3D163413343
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Buncombe Age-Friendly Senior Centers
SUMMARY:HCCBG Advisory Committee
LOCATION:To view meetings via live streaming\, please go to <br><a href=
 "https://engage.buncombecounty.org/x1728" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
  title="https://engage.buncombecounty.org/x1728">engage.buncombecounty.o
 rg&#8230\;</a>.  Meetings can be watched at a later time for your conven
 ience.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T163000
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:FALSE
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Event Type";ID=21;TYPE=number:Children &amp\;
  Family Services
DTSTAMP:20230818T161720Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>The Home and Community Care Block Grant Advisory Committ
 ee meets monthly.&#160\; The Home and Community Care Block Grant Advisor
 y Committee makes grant recommendations to the Board of Commissioners re
 garding allocations of Home and Community Care Block Grant funding and C
 ounty Aging Services funding yearly. &#160\;During the other months\, th
 e Committee reviews provider spending\, annual reporting\, and discusses
  gaps within the aging services network.&#160\; This is an open meeting 
 and anyone is welcome to listen in.&#160\;
CATEGORIES:Age Friendly
